    "field": "Decadal climate variability",
    "problem": "Characterizing decadal-scale oceanic climate variability is challenging due to the limited duration and sparse, irregular data coverage of the observational record, which hinders robust assessments of its patterns, timescales, and governing mechanisms.",
    "method": "This paper characterizes decadal-scale climate variability by adopting a basin-specific approach to analyze historical sea surface temperature anomalies, defining regional indices for major oceans, and regressing global data onto them to reveal associated spatial patterns and temporal relationships.",
    "task": "The task is to provide an overview of the main phenomena of decadal-scale sea surface temperature variability in the historical observational record, discussing proposed interpretations, causal mechanisms, and outstanding research questions.",
